      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:38 GMT</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>77</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.3.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font: 13px/1.45 -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 10px 14px; }
ul { padding-left: 18px; margin: 4px 0; } li { margin: 4px 0; }
h3 { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin: 12px 0 4px; }
code { font: 12px ui-monospace, monospace; }
</style><ul>
<li>The screen no longer dims or goes to sleep in the middle of a film. While a video plays (in the player or the mini player) Mezzanine keeps the Mac awake; paused, closed or casting to a TV, the Mac sleeps as usual.</li>
<li>Remote control from Plex apps is now off by default (Settings ▸ Playback): Plex&#x27;s current iPhone and Android apps only cast to Google Cast devices, not to Plex players like Mezzanine.</li>
</ul>]]></description>
